      <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Is a job simulation as good as an internship?</div><div class="faq-a">They are good at different things. An internship gives you context, mentorship, a network, and a reference a simulation cannot fully replicate. A simulation gives you a fast, accessible way to produce evaluated proof of skill. The best use is to combine them, or to use a simulation to build proof when an internship is out of reach.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Can a job simulation replace an internship?</div><div class="faq-a">It can replace the proof an internship produces, which is the part recruiters care about most, but not the relationships and reference. If you cannot get an internship, evaluated work from a simulation is the closest substitute for the hiring signal, built on your own schedule.</div></div>
